       <section anchor="purpose" numbered="true" removeInRFC="false" toc="include" pn="section-2.3">
         <name slugifiedName="name-purpose">Purpose</name>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.3-1">As described in [1], there are now a number of services implementing
-dialup roaming, and the number of Internet Service Providers involved
-in roaming consortia is increasing rapidly.</t>
-        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.3-2">In order to be able to offer roaming capability, one of the
-requirements is to be able to identify the user's home authentication
-server.  For use in roaming, this function is accomplished via the
-Network Access Identifier (NAI) submitted by the user to the NAS in
