-to determine the tunnel endpoint.</t>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.3-1">As described in <xref target="1" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="1"/>, there are now a number of services implementing dialup roaming, and the number of Internet Service Providers involved in roaming consortia is increasing rapidly.</t>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.3-2">In order to be able to offer roaming capability, one of the requirements is to be able to identify the user's home authentication server.  For use in roaming, this function is accomplished via the Network Access Identifier (NAI) submitted by the user to the NAS in the initial PPP authentication.  It is also expected that NASes will use the NAI as part of the process of opening a new tunnel, in order to determine the tunnel endpoint.</t>
       </section>
