-NAIs <bcp14>MUST</bcp14> support an NAI length of at least 72 octets.</t>
+        <t indent="0" pn="section-2.4-1">As proposed in this document, the Network Access Identifier is of the form user@realm.  Please note that while the user portion of the NAI conforms to the BNF described in <xref target="5" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="5"/>, the BNF of the realm portion allows the realm to begin with a digit, which is not permitted by the BNF described in <xref target="4" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="4"/>. This change was made to reflect current practice; although not permitted by the BNF described in <xref target="4" format="default" sectionFormat="of" derivedContent="4"/>, FQDNs such as 3com.com are commonly used, and accepted by current software.</t>
